STATE SAFETY

Before demo playback:

- Save or isolate current synthetic app state.
- Prepare deterministic fictional data.
- Validate prerequisites.
- Confirm the scenario can execute.
- Show an unmistakable Demo Mode indicator.

During playback:

- Keep record identities consistent.
- Prevent duplicate mutations.
- Preserve correct clinical state transitions.
- Respect role/facility scope.
- Stop when an assertion fails.

After playback:

- Offer Replay, Practice or Exit.
- Preserve or restore data according to explicit demo controls.
- Do not corrupt unrelated application records.

When replaying a previous step, restore a checkpoint instead of blindly repeating a save operation.

CLINICAL APPROVAL SAFETY

Scripted demo approvals must be clearly labeled as fictional demonstrations.

They must not create real clinician signatures or real clinical orders.

In regular application mode, an authorized human must approve clinical actions.

No real patient information, external prescriptions, live diagnostic orders or clinical messages are allowed in synthetic tutorial playback.

